    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Thirty-seven, I decided, was old enough. These days, most people learn to drive in their 20s, but somehow, I had never gotten "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "around to",
            "zh": "抽出时间做"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it. And so, one morning last fall, I found myself trying to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "master",
            "ref": "v-master"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the foot movements that are required to hit something called the “biting point”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "That’s when your left foot, on the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "clutch",
            "zh": "离合器踏板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", perfectly balances with your right foot, on the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "gas",
            "zh": "油门踏板"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", allowing the car to "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "pull away"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " smoothly. My friends considered my decision to learn on a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "manual transmission",
            "zh": "手动变速器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to be stupid. Didn’t I know that in a few years, almost all cars would be automatic? Well, I just wanted to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "challenge",
            "ref": "v-challenge"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " myself. If I never do anything that challenges me, how can I grow?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The first time my "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "instructor",
            "ref": "v-instructor"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Gemma, opened the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "hood",
            "zh": "引擎盖"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", I looked closely at the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "brake fluid",
            "zh": "制动液"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "radiator",
            "zh": "散热器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "oil reservoirs",
            "zh": "油罐"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and felt excited. That excitement, though, lasted only about three minutes into the first lesson. Every time the car picked up speed, I felt nervous and hit the brakes. “We made it to nearly four miles per hour,” said Gemma. After the lesson, I felt down. I hit my head against the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "steering wheel",
            "zh": "方向盘"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Until that moment, I hadn’t realised that that was where the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "horn",
            "zh": "喇叭"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was located. I felt like a clown."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After three months of daily practice, I was, at last, ready to get off the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "beginner’s slopes",
            "zh": "坡"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and onto the real roads. “Wow! This is freedom!” I exclaimed as I stepped on the gas. “This is still only 18 miles per hour,” Gemma said. “Look how many cars are behind us.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I sped up and held my breath. Each time, it was a little easier. The joy—and sadness—of learning is that what was once challenging becomes boring."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Finally, I was ready for my test. The night before, I was so nervous that I woke up every hour. Honestly, I had expected to fail—and for this article to end with a teachable moment: Failure brings even more personal growth. But I passed. When the examiner gave me the news, I felt a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "rare",
            "ref": "v-rare"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " sense of achievement. I was bad at driving, but I did it anyway. That somehow meant more than "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "excellence",
            "ref": "v-excellence"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I’m bad at so many other things. What should I try next?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
